work_units.notes:
RankTable.tsx:21-25 - ordinal() only special-cases 1/2/3; everything
else falls through to `${n}th`.  Renders "21th", "22nd"→"22th" for
n >= 21 that end in 1/2/3 (except 11/12/13 which are correctly "th").
Unlikely with current platform counts but technically wrong.

Fix: standard ordinal suffix rule -
  const suffixes = ["th","st","nd","rd"];
  const v = n % 100;
  return `${n}${suffixes[(v - 20) % 10] ?? suffixes[v] ?? suffixes[0]}`;

BenchmarkIndex.tsx:383-386 - The Histogram, Box Plot, and CDF tabs are
unconditionally shown (hardcoded true).  When all platform timings are
null or empty, clicking these tabs shows a blank section because each
chart guards internally and returns null.  The Percentiles, Power, Phases,
and Cost tabs are already data-gated.

Fix: add a `hasTimings` guard:
  const hasTimings = s.platforms.some(
    (p) => Object.values(p.timings).some((v) => v !== null && v > 0)
  );
Then use hasTimings for the histogram/distribution/cdf entries.
